{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113279","id":3054193103,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc62C0nP","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113279","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113279.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113279.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113279","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113279/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113279/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113279/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/acefbbbbcdadc23b229ab91ebd52385551a8fcfc","number":113279,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add support for profiling GDScript with tracy.","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"- Supersedes #112707\r\n- Follow-up of #104851 \r\n\r\nThis PR allows users to profile their games' GDScript functions using the [tracy profiler](https://github.com/wolfpld/tracy).\r\nIt is a collaborative work between @enetheru and me.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1300\" height=\"484\" alt=\"SCR-20251128-nknw\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/17b17a9b-d305-4c39-8a73-956ec951a8ca\" />\r\n\r\nUsers can use the tracy instructions on the docs (currently [in PR form](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-docs/pull/11484), soon available [here](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine_details/development/debugging/using_cpp_profilers.html)) to start profiling their games. Note that profiling with tracy requires recompiling the engine.\r\n\r\nI've profiled tps-demo for about ~10 minutes straight, and both Godot and tracy stay responsive, without any apparent slowdowns or leaks.\r\n\r\n### Approach\r\n\r\nTracy profile zones generally make use of `constexpr tracy::SourceLocationData *`, which are passed to the profiling macros. With this trick, tracy can introspect millions of events, because it only needs to store a start location, and end location, and a pointer to the `SourceLocationData`.\r\n\r\nWhile tracy supports dynamic source locations / strings, effectively it just copies the contents and leaks it. This works, but is wasteful, because tons of data is leaked. A [previous implementation](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3BIteSVcO28) (by the developers of Halls of Torment) ran into limitations with this approach, because it led to gigabytes of data filling up after a few seconds of profiling (I don't know for sure they used tracy's leaky approach, but it would match the observations).\r\n\r\nInstead of using tracy's dynamic source location API, this PR [interns](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interning_(computer_science)) source locations for `GDScriptFunction` objects, and leaks those instead. This means that every function is only leaked once, instead of once per call, which allows us to profile for much, much longer. This takes inspiration from `StringName`'s interning approach.\r\nThe implementation is fully contained in the tracy glue internals, and doesn't affect games that don't compile with tracy. It is further contained to `.cpp` files including `profiling.h`, so recompiling with a profiler attached stays trivial. \r\n\r\n(it would be possible to attach a `void *` to `GDScriptFunction` instances instead of interning `SourceLocationData`. This would be faster, but it wouldn't be self-contained anymore. In the future, if people start running into performance overhead from the profiler, we can amend the implementation to do this instead).\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","description":"","color":"447777","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12939969,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AxXLB","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/23","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23/labels","number":23,"state":"closed","title":"4.6","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5